<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Subartu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Subartu was an ancient name for a region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. Accounts of the Babylonian Empire list it among the members of a coalition defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>. This victory showed his ability to confront multiple powers simultaneously.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/subartu.jpg" alt="Subartu" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Middle_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur (talk) derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empire_akkad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
